[62.300302, "o", "----- context -----\r\n[1] (source: demo-app/sample-data/pgvector.md#0)\r\n# pgvector\r\n\r\npgvector is a PostgreSQL extension for vector similarity search. It adds the\r\n`vector` data type and distance operators: `<->` (Euclidean), `<#>` (negative\r\ninner product) and `<=>` (cosine distance).\r\n\r\nIt supports exact nearest-neighbour search and two approximate index types:\r\nIVFFlat, which partitions vectors into lists, and HNSW, which builds a\r\nmulti-layer graph and offers a better speed/recall trade-off at the cost of\r\nslower index builds and more memory.\r\n\r\n[2] (source: demo-app/sample-data/cloudnative-pg.md#0)\r\n# CloudNativePG\r\n\r\nCloudNativePG is a Kubernetes operator that manages the full lifecycle of\r\nPostgreSQL clusters: bootstrap, high availability with automated failover,\r\nrolling updates, backups and point-in-time recovery, and monitoring through a\r\nPrometheus exporter built into every instance.\r\n\r\nA cluster is described declaratively with the `Cluster` custom resource. The\r\noperator creates one primary and, optionally, a number of streaming replicas.\r\nApplications connect through three services: `-rw` (primary only), `-ro`\r\n(replicas only) and `-r` (any instance).\r\n\r\nExtensions such as pgvector can be enabled with `CREATE EXTENSION`, either at\r\nbootstrap time or declaratively through the `Database` resource.\r\n-------------------\r\n"]
[88.604305, "o", "\r\npgvector supports two approximate index types: IVFFlat, which partitions vectors into lists, and HNSW, which builds a multi-layer graph.\r\n\r\nSources:\r\n  [1] demo-app/sample-data/pgvector.md#0  (similarity 0.822)\r\n  [2] demo-app/sample-data/cloudnative-pg.md#0  (similarity 0.600)\r\n"]
